  "en": "No — being roughly right every day beats being exact and quitting.\\n\\n• Hand estimates work fine: palm ≈ one protein serving · fist ≈ one veg serving · cupped hand ≈ one carb serving · thumb ≈ one fat serving\\n• Log carefully for 3–5 days at the start to learn your own numbers, then loosen to rough logging\\n• If counting makes you anxious or guilty about food, switch to behaviours instead (protein every meal, half a plate of veg, fewer sweet drinks)\\n\\nThe goal is control of the big picture, not a perfect score every day"
