  "en": "The best time is the one you will actually keep — the rest is a small difference.\\n\\n• Morning: fewer things can hijack the plan, and it is done for the day; you just need a longer warm-up\\n• Evening: strength and body temperature are usually better for heavy lifting, but work and errands get in the way more\\n• If training late leaves you unable to sleep, move it earlier or ease off in late sessions\\n• Keeping the same time slot builds the habit faster than rotating",
